  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency and Recovery Response to (IDPs) in Ibba County, Western Equatoria State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is to improve the livelihood of the IDPS in Ibba by supporting them with the basic things prioritizing cash, non-food items, some agriculture inputs, peace building, training on business skills (VSLA groups for women). The conflict that has been in the Western Equatoria State has made the community more vulnerable thus creating humanitarian crisis. The main challenges for the IDPs, orphans and the host communities is lack of basic things like shelter, food, water, medicines and other non-food items. This situation created by the violence calls for the intervention and the result of the need assessment carried out by the Joint Assessment team (CMMB, LM international, UNFAO, STO, RRC, Rescue Initiative, UNICEF, WVI, Amref, CARD and YEDA) from12 &amp; 17 November 2025 states that there is NO ongoing and/or planned response to the needs of the IDPs who live in Ibba.  Among the things recommended by the Joint Assessment Team are cash distributions, distribution of seeds, agricultural tools before the next faming season, Distribution of emergency shelter items (plastic sheets, rubber ropes and local shelter materials), Distribution of NFIs (kitchen sets and NFI bags), including bedding items (sleeping mats, mosquito nets, and blankets).</narrative>
  </description>
